WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.882
When a user types into an input prompt Python
receives the response as text This

00:00:05.895 --> 00:00:11.262
is true even if the person typed digits that look
like a number If we

00:00:11.288 --> 00:00:16.672
want to use that input in arithmetic we usually need
to convert it The integer

00:00:16.699 --> 00:00:21.172
function creates a whole number and the float
function creates a numeric value that can

00:00:21.199 --> 00:00:27.901
include decimals This pattern appears far beyond
keyboard input Data

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:33.862
from forms CSV files web pages and APIs can also
arrive as text One

00:00:33.875 --> 00:00:38.283
of the first tasks in data preparation is often
checking whether values have the correct

00:00:38.309 --> 00:00:39.849
type for the work we want to do
